\fs66\fsmilli33333 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf3 \strokec3 Disease Atlas and Ciaran Space Ontology Comparison\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa346\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \AppleTypeServices \cf4 \strokec4 A practical comparison of the live Geo ontology used in Disease Atlas and the ontology currently used in Ciaran's metabolic-model space, with recommendations for reuse, provenance, source identifiers, and cross-space interoperability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf5 \strokec5 Prepared from live Geo queries on April 20, 2026. Spaces reviewed: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.geobrowser.io/space/141d3ace705feabc04d50c78bbf7226e"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \strokec6 Disease Atlas}} and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.geobrowser.io/space/aec359295ff90d00aea6696f0ddb1bbc"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \strokec6 Ciaran's space}}.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 Executive summary.
\f1\b0  Ciaran's space is a metabolic-network style graph, probably imported from BiGG / an E. coli K-12 MG1655 genome-scale model. Disease Atlas is a disease-mechanism and evidence graph.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb8 The biggest ontology issue in Ciaran's space is not the metabolism-specific terms. Those are mostly reasonable. The biggest gaps are provenance and reuse:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa53\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec9 Gene
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7  is duplicated locally instead of reusing Health's 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Gene
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 .\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa53\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf7 \cb8 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 There are no 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Source
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 , 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Dataset
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 , or 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Paper
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7  entities.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb8 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 There is no source provenance linking entities or relations back to BiGG, the model, or the paper.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa53\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec9 BiGG ID
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7  is useful, but it is overloaded across reactions, metabolites, genes, and compartments.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa53\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf7 \cb8 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 Relation entities are mostly not named or provenance-backed in the way Disease Atlas evidence claims are.\cb1 \
