\f0\b\fs40 \cf11 \strokec11 Main Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 Do not make Disease Atlas absorb Ciaran's metabolism ontology yet. Instead, make both spaces interoperable through shared 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Gene
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 , shared provenance, shared source identifiers, and source-backed relation entities.\cb1 \
\cb8 That gives a clean bridge:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Disease -> Gene
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7  in Disease Atlas\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Gene -> Reaction -> Metabolite
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7  in Ciaran's space\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb8 Once Ciaran's genes reuse Health 
\f2\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf9 \cb10 \strokec9 Gene
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14933 \cf7 \cb8 \strokec7 , a future dashboard can click a gene from Disease Atlas and discover metabolic reactions from Ciaran's graph without merging the two spaces or overloading Disease Atlas with metabolic-model details.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa186\partightenfactor0

